WEBVTT

00:00.403 --> 00:02.671
Say we need this box back at the assembly line.

00:06.329 --> 00:11.136
First, the Composer reads the robot's code and connects the matching drone

00:11.316 --> 00:12.450
and camera modules.

00:12.875 --> 00:15.002
A person checks the supported skills.

00:15.440 --> 00:19.203
Then it creates an RCD file and an embodied agent.

00:23.316 --> 00:25.352
That agent knows what its robot can do.

00:25.777 --> 00:27.053
It runs on the workstation.

00:27.465 --> 00:29.012
Stopping stays on the robot.

00:32.303 --> 00:35.525
The drone searches the factory and finds the red box.

00:35.924 --> 00:38.605
It adds that observation to Hive's shared map:

00:39.120 --> 00:40.821
what it is, and where it is.

00:41.234 --> 00:43.282
The rover only sees in grayscale,

00:43.566 --> 00:45.589
but now it knows which box to collect.

00:50.303 --> 00:52.661
The Executive sends the rover to pick it up.

00:53.048 --> 00:56.012
There's no safe carrying space, so it brings in the mule.

01:02.303 --> 01:05.331
The rover loads the box, then checks it with its camera.

01:05.744 --> 01:08.579
That fresh observation updates the shared map.

01:09.004 --> 01:10.383
Only then does the mule head back.

01:16.290 --> 01:19.795
At the assembly line, the overhead camera checks the box.

01:20.221 --> 01:21.986
The fixed arm moves it onto the conveyor,

01:22.424 --> 01:23.661
and confirms the delivery.
